 "stimulus_html": "<p>Suppose we have data that are normally distributed with mean 500 and standard deviation 100. What proportions of the data fall in these ranges?</p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 542770,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>300 to 500</p>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>47.5%</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Consider these boundaries on the normal curve.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>mean − 3 SD</th>\n<th>mean − 2 SD</th>\n<th>mean − 1 SD</th>\n<th>mean</th>\n<th>mean + 1 SD</th>\n<th>mean + 2 SD</th>\n<th>mean + 3 SD</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>500 − 300</td>\n<td>500 − 200</td>\n<td>500 − 100</td>\n<td>500</td>\n<td>500 + 100</td>\n<td>500 + 200</td>\n<td>500 + 300</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>200</td>\n<td>300</td>\n<td>400</td>\n<td>500</td>\n<td>600</td>\n<td>700</td>\n<td>800</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Sketch the curve and shade in the area between 300 and 500.</p>\n<p>If it were 300 to 700, it would be 95%.</p>\n<p>However, it is just half of that.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"95 \\div 2 = 47.5\\%\"></span></p>\n<p>The 68–95–99.7 Rule tells you that 47.5% of the data values are between 300 and 500.</p>\n<p>47.5%</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 542771,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>600 to 800</p>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>15.85%</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Consider these boundaries on the normal curve.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>mean − 3 SD</th>\n<th>mean − 2 SD</th>\n<th>mean − 1 SD</th>\n<th>mean</th>\n<th>mean + 1 SD</th>\n<th>mean + 2 SD</th>\n<th>mean + 3 SD</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>500 − 300</td>\n<td>500 − 200</td>\n<td>500 − 100</td>\n<td>500</td>\n<td>500 + 100</td>\n<td>500 + 200</td>\n<td>500 + 300</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>200</td>\n<td>300</td>\n<td>400</td>\n<td>500</td>\n<td>600</td>\n<td>700</td>\n<td>800</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Sketch the curve and shade in the area between 600 and 800.</p>\n<p>What if it were 500 to 800?</p>\n<p>If it were 200 to 800, it would be 99.7%.</p>\n<p>However, 500 to 800 is just half of that.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"99.7 \\div 2 = 49.85\\%\"></span></p>\n<p>49.85% of the data falls between 500 and 800.</p>\n<p>Now you need to subtract off the data between 500 and 600.</p>\n<p>Since 600 is one SD from the mean, you know there is 34% of the area between 500 and 600.</p>\n<p>Subtract 34% from 49.85% to get 15.85%.</p>\n<p>The 68–95–99.7 Rule tells you that 15.85% of the data values are between 600 and 800.</p>\n<p>15.85%</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 542772,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>400 to 700</p>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>81.5%</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Consider these boundaries on the normal curve.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>mean − 3 SD</th>\n<th>mean − 2 SD</th>\n<th>mean − 1 SD</th>\n<th>mean</th>\n<th>mean + 1 SD</th>\n<th>mean + 2 SD</th>\n<th>mean + 3 SD</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>500 − 300</td>\n<td>500 − 200</td>\n<td>500 − 100</td>\n<td>500</td>\n<td>500 + 100</td>\n<td>500 + 200</td>\n<td>500 + 300</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>200</td>\n<td>300</td>\n<td>400</td>\n<td>500</td>\n<td>600</td>\n<td>700</td>\n<td>800</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Sketch the curve and shade in the area between 400 and 700.</p>\n<p>Handle the portion left of the peak and right of the peak separately.</p>\n<p>Left of the peak is half of the one-standard deviation from the curve portion. This is half of 68%, or 34% of the area.</p>\n<p>Right of the peak is half of the two-standard deviation from the curve portion. This is half of 95%, or 47.5% of the area.</p>\n<p>Add 34% and 47.5% to get 81.5%.</p>\n<p>The 68–95–99.7 Rule tells you that 81.5% of the data values are between 400 and 700.</p>\n<p>81.5%</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
